| `make secret-scan` `[local]` | Scans every commit config/project.json `secrets.scanner.history_log_opts` reaches with the scanner `make secrets-install` recorded, through `scripts/scan_secrets.py --history`, and prints each finding as `file:line rule commit`, never the value. It is a `make verify` goal, so a credential a `--no-verify` commit carried in is red there and in CI. | `make secret-scan` | [`secrets.scanner.history_log_opts`](settings.md#configprojectjson), [`secrets.scanner.exclusions`](settings.md#configprojectjson), [`secrets.scanner.record_file`](settings.md#configprojectjson), [`PY`](settings.md#make-variables) | Judges shapes the scanner's default rules know, not a value under a name no rule matches: the keyed gate, `tests/integration/test_committed_secrets_gate.py`, judges names. Exits 11 (`BACKEND_ABSENT`) with no record or one naming another rev or build, never a skip, and 13 before the first commit. A history already pushed stays exposed: a finding means rotate the credential (limits-and-troubleshooting.md, "A credential was committed"). Not for the staged diff: the pre-commit hook runs `--staged-or-history`. A record path escaping the project is exit 14 before scan temporaries are created. | [deterministic-checks.md](../guides/deterministic-checks.md) | always |
